(3.3 API interfaces) Tj
T*
(|  Component  |  Method and route  |  Result / error handling  |) Tj
T*
(| --- | --- | --- |) Tj
T*
(|  Search  |  GET /api/trains/search  |  Schedule options; validation errors for invalid query  |) Tj
T*
(|  Booking  |  POST /api/bookings  |  Pending booking and PNR; validation/availability/conflict) Tj
T*
(errors  |) Tj
T*
(|  Payment  |  POST /api/bookings/{id}/pay  |  Simulated confirmation; unauthorized, invalid or) Tj
T*
(expired hold errors  |) Tj
T*
(|  Cancellation  |  POST /api/bookings/{id}/cancel  |  Cancellation and refund details;) Tj
T*
(eligibility/ownership errors  |) Tj
T*
(|  Admin  |  PATCH /api/admin/trains/{id}  |  Updated train; role, validation and duplicate errors ) Tj
T*
(|) Tj
T*
(|  Operations  |  GET /api/health/db  |  200 on connection, 503 when database unavailable  |) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3.4 Error handling, logging and monitoring) Tj
T*
(Views map expected domain failures to controlled HTTP errors. Database outages return) Tj
T*
(service-unavailable responses without raw SQL exception details. /api/health and /api/health/db) Tj
T*
(support basic checks; production alerting, audit retention and automated failover have not been) Tj
T*
(established.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3.5 User experience) Tj
T*
(Passenger screens cover authentication, train search, booking, simulated payment, status/history and) Tj
T*
(cancellation. Admin screens cover operations and record inspection. Automated browser checks exist;) Tj
T*
(accessibility certification is not claimed.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3.6 Architecture decisions and open issues) Tj
T*
(Use the existing schema, preserve row-lock ordering, keep transactions inside services, and avoid) Tj
T*
(duplicated business logic in views. Open limitations: real gateway integration, provider delivery,) Tj
T*
(production monitoring, live database integration tests and formal performance measurements.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
